<article class="env-lemma" id="0A79">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A79">Lemma <span data-tag="0A79">48.9.6</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes. Assume $X$ is a locally Noetherian. Then $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (\mathcal{O}_ Z, -)$ maps $D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ into $D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Z)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is local on $X$, hence we may assume that $X$ is affine. Say $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and $Z = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ with $A$ Noetherian and $A \to B$ surjective. In this case, we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0A78" data-tag="0A78">48.9.5</a> to translate the question into algebra. The corresponding algebra result is a consequence of Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A72" data-tag="0A72">47.13.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>